{"post_stream":{"posts":[{"id":503405,"name":"Wes Anderson","username":"Wes_Anderson","avatar_template":"https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/w/0ea827/{size}.png","created_at":"2026-09-29T12:41:27.317Z","cooked":"\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-503405-where-does-the-bug-appear-featureproduct-1\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-503405-where-does-the-bug-appear-featureproduct-1\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eWhere does the bug appear (feature/product)?\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGrok Bot\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-503405-describe-the-bug-2\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-503405-describe-the-bug-2\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eDescribe the Bug\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eEvery link I put in an email through the Gmail connector is saved and sent as a Google redirect instead of the real address. For example, \u003ca href=\"https://smartanimaltraining.com/pages/support\" class=\"inline-onebox\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003eSupport – Pet Tutor by Smart Animal Training Systems\u003c/a\u003e becomes \u003ca href=\"https://www.google.com/url?q=https://smartanimaltraining.com/pages/support\u0026amp;source=gmail\u0026amp;ust=1790770503097000\u0026amp;sa=E\" class=\"inline-onebox\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003eRedirect Notice\u003c/a\u003e. The rewritten link appears both as the visible text and as the actual link target, so customers receive the redirect, can hit Google’s “you’re leaving” warning, and save the wrong link. Links that contain placeholders like  come out broken. Emails I write myself in Gmail on the same account are not affected. We use this mailbox for customer support, so every Welcome letter and support reply with a link goes out this way.\u003cbr\u003e\nexample:\u003cbr\u003e\nLink: \u003ca href=\"https://cursor.com\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003ehttps://cursor.com\u003c/a\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\nLink: \u003ca href=\"https://www.google.com/url?q=https://cursor.com\u0026amp;source=gmail\u0026amp;ust=1790771987631000\u0026amp;sa=E\" class=\"inline-onebox\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003eRedirect Notice\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-503405-steps-to-reproduce-3\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-503405-steps-to-reproduce-3\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eSteps to Reproduce\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eOn Sep 29, 2026, I had my Grok Bot create five test drafts to myself, then read each one back with get_draft in RAW format:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ePlain-text body with a full https:// URL: wrapped.\u003cbr\u003e\nhtmlBody with \u003ca href=\"https://...\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003e: the href was wrapped.\u003cbr\u003e\nhtmlBody link with different visible text, plus a plain-text alternative: both parts wrapped.\u003cbr\u003e\nA bare domain with no https://: Gmail turned it into a link and wrapped it (as http://).\u003cbr\u003e\nhtmlBody with an HTML-entity-encoded href: still wrapped. Sending through send_message also wraps links. A message sent on Sep 28 arrived with both of its links rewritten and broken.\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://...\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003e\n\u003c/a\u003e\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://...\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-503405-expected-behavior-4\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-503405-expected-behavior-4\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eExpected Behavior\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eLinks are stored and sent exactly as written, the same as when composing in Gmail.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-503405-operating-system-5\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-503405-operating-system-5\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eOperating System\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWindows 10/11\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-503405-version-information-6\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-503405-version-information-6\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eVersion Information\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGok Bot 0.62.0\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-503405-for-ai-issues-which-model-did-you-use-7\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-503405-for-ai-issues-which-model-did-you-use-7\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eFor AI issues: which model did you use?\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eNot model-related. The rewriting happens in the connector.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-503405-additional-information-8\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-503405-additional-information-8\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eAdditional Information\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSeveral public GitHub reports describe the same behavior with other AI assistants’ Gmail connectors, starting around June 5, 2026 and still open, for example anthropics/claude-code#66010 and #94247. A commenter there reported that a community Gmail tool that calls the Gmail API directly produced clean links.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-503405-does-this-stop-you-from-using-cursor-9\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-503405-does-this-stop-you-from-using-cursor-9\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eDoes this stop you from using Cursor\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eYes - Cursor is unusable\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":1,"post_type":1,"posts_count":2,"updated_at":"2026-09-29T15:22:24.074Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":17,"reads":3,"readers_count":2,"score":85.6,"yours":false,"topic_id":173321,"topic_slug":"grok-bot-gmail-connector-user-gmail-rewrites-every-link-into-google-com-url-redirects-on-create-draft-and-send-message","display_username":"Wes Anderson","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":2,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"link_counts":[{"url":"https://www.google.com/url?q=https://cursor.com\u0026source=gmail\u0026ust=1790771987631000\u0026sa=E","internal":false,"reflection":false,"title":"Redirect Notice","clicks":1},{"url":"https://smartanimaltraining.com/pages/support","internal":false,"reflection":false,"title":"Support – Pet Tutor by Smart Animal Training Systems","clicks":0},{"url":"https://www.google.com/url?q=https://smartanimaltraining.com/pages/support\u0026source=gmail\u0026ust=1790770503097000\u0026sa=E","internal":false,"reflection":false,"title":"Redirect Notice","clicks":0},{"url":"https://cursor.com","internal":false,"reflection":false,"title":"AI Coding Agent for Building Ambitious Software | Cursor","clicks":0},{"url":"https://...","internal":false,"reflection":false,"clicks":0}],"read":true,"user_title":null,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":136160,"hidden":false,"trust_level":1,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/grok-bot-gmail-connector-user-gmail-rewrites-every-link-into-google-com-url-redirects-on-create-draft-and-send-message/173321/1","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null,"can_vote":false},{"id":503499,"name":"Colin","username":"Colin","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/colin/{size}/90452_2.png","created_at":"2026-09-29T15:22:00.893Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eHey \u003ca class=\"mention\" href=\"/u/wes_anderson\"\u003e@Wes_Anderson\u003c/a\u003e, thanks for the report and for the test drafts you ran.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eYou’re right that this happens in the Gmail connection itself, not in how Grok Bot writes the email: links sent through the connector are saved with Google’s redirect wrapper, whether they come in as plain text or as HTML. This is a known issue we’re already tracking, and I’ve added your report to it.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIn the meantime, for any email that contains links, the safest option is to have Grok Bot write the text in chat (or save the draft without the links) and then paste the message or add the links yourself in Gmail before sending. As you noticed, emails composed directly in Gmail keep their links exactly as written. I’d also avoid having the bot send link-containing emails directly with send_message until this is sorted out.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":5,"post_type":1,"posts_count":2,"updated_at":"2026-09-29T15:22:00.893Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":0,"reads":3,"readers_count":2,"score":15.6,"yours":false,"topic_id":173321,"topic_slug":"grok-bot-gmail-connector-user-gmail-rewrites-every-link-into-google-com-url-redirects-on-create-draft-and-send-message","display_username":"Colin","primary_group_name":"CursorStaff","flair_name":"CursorStaff","flair_url":"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/original/3X/a/d/ad08adc640929ae1e98be69dab1ad0844cee99a0.png","flair_bg_color":"","flair_color":"","flair_group_id":42,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":"Community Support Engineer","title_is_group":false,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[{"id":2,"count":1}],"moderator":true,"admin":true,"staff":true,"user_id":87436,"hidden":false,"trust_level":3,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/grok-bot-gmail-connector-user-gmail-rewrites-every-link-into-google-com-url-redirects-on-create-draft-and-send-message/173321/5","reactions":[{"id":"heart","type":"emoji","count":1}],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":1,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null}],"s